          <Pad Id="O0Uv21qrxw1P8sfwxvk7r6" Bounds="321,329,690,210" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Every collidable (Body, Static, Character) carries exactly one ICollider, which describes its complete shape.&#xD;&#xA;Only three types implement ICollider: CompoundCollider, MeshCollider and EmptyCollider.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The shape colliders (Box, Sphere, Capsule, Cylinder, Triangle, ConvexHull) are of type ColliderBase.&#xD;&#xA;They are convex shapes that only exist as children of a compound, which is why they have Position Local,&#xD;&#xA;Rotation Local and Mass pins. The Colliders pin wraps them into a component owned CompoundCollider&#xD;&#xA;automatically, even a single shape. Mass and center of mass are computed from the children.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;A mesh cannot be part of a compound: it is not convex and brings its own triangle acceleration structure,&#xD;&#xA;so it is a complete shape by itself. MeshCollider and EmptyCollider therefore connect to the&#xD;&#xA;Collider Override pin instead of the Colliders pin.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
